2026-11-06T14:53:17.4997660Z 
2026-11-06T14:53:17.4997800Z LLD and LLDB are now provided in separate formulae:
2026-11-06T14:53:17.4998260Z   brew install lld
2026-11-06T14:53:17.4998620Z   brew install lldb
2026-11-06T14:53:17.4998740Z 
2026-11-06T14:53:17.4999010Z Z3 solver support will be removed in LLVM 24 as it is unsupported upstream,
2026-11-06T14:53:17.4999780Z see https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/205370
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5000080Z 
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5000340Z Using `clang`, `clang++`, etc., requires a CLT installation at `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`.
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5008970Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5011090Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5011340Z 
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5011480Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5012040Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5012380Z 
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5012640Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5013590Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5014330Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5014860Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5015280Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5015540Z 
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5015940Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5016390Z 
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5016540Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5017140Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5017720Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5017960Z 
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5018080Z If you need to have llvm first in your PATH, run:
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5018710Z   printf '%s\n' export\ PATH\=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:\$PATH >> /Users/runner/.bash_profile
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5019070Z 
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5019680Z For compilers to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5020630Z   export LDFLAGS=-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5021620Z   export CPPFLAGS=-I/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/include
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5022770Z 
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5022960Z For cmake to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-11-06T14:53:17.5023280Z   export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm
